{{!
    @template mod_rememberme/report_difficulty

    Per question difficulty across the cohort, hardest first.

    The purpose is finding defective questions. Difficulty is a per learner
    quantity, so an item that is difficult for one learner is simply difficult
    for that learner; an item that is difficult for nearly everybody is usually
    badly worded, ambiguous, or has a wrong answer key.

    The questionname value arrives already passed through format_string(), so it
    is filtered, escaped HTML and is rendered unescaped on purpose. Every other
    value is escaped by the template engine.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasrows Boolean Whether there is any data at all
    * hasflagged Boolean Whether any question crossed the flag threshold
    * flaggedcount Number How many questions crossed it
    * threshold String The mean difficulty at which a question is flagged
    * minlearners Number How many learners must have attempted an item before it can be flagged
    * rows Array of rows, each with:
        * questionname String The question name, already format_string()ed
        * learners Number How many learners have memory state for this item
        * meandifficulty String Mean difficulty across those learners
        * meanstability String Mean stability in days
        * meanlapses String Mean lapses per learner
        * reps Number Total successful recalls across the cohort
        * flagged Boolean Whether this row is worth a teacher's attention

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasrows": true,
        "hasflagged": true,
        "flaggedcount": 1,
        "threshold": "7.0",
        "minlearners": 3,
        "rows": [
            {
                "questionname": "Which of these is a noun?",
                "learners": 24,
                "meandifficulty": "8.41",
                "meanstability": "1.90",
                "meanlapses": "3.10",
                "reps": 41,
                "flagged": true
            },
            {
                "questionname": "Translate: the red house",
                "learners": 22,
                "meandifficulty": "4.02",
                "meanstability": "17.30",
                "meanlapses": "0.40",
                "reps": 96,
                "flagged": false
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="mod_rememberme-report mod_rememberme-report-difficulty">
    <p class="text-muted">{{#str}}reportdifficulty_help, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</p>

    {{#hasflagged}}
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="status">
            {{#str}}difficultyflagged, mod_rememberme, {"count": {{flaggedcount}}, "threshold": "{{threshold}}", "learners": {{minlearners}}}{{/str}}
        </div>
    {{/hasflagged}}

    {{#hasrows}}
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-striped generaltable">
            <caption>{{#str}}reportdifficultycaption, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}question, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}meandifficulty, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}learners, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}meanlapses, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}meanstability, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}reviews, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {{#rows}}
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row" class="font-weight-normal">
                        {{{questionname}}}
                        {{#flagged}}
                            <span class="badge badge-warning bg-warning text-dark ms-1">{{#str}}flagreview, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</span>
                        {{/flagged}}
                    </th>
                    <td>{{meandifficulty}}</td>
                    <td>{{learners}}</td>
                    <td>{{meanlapses}}</td>
                    <td>{{meanstability}}</td>
                    <td>{{reps}}</td>
                </tr>
                {{/rows}}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    {{/hasrows}}
    {{^hasrows}}
        <p class="text-muted">{{#str}}reportnodata, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</p>
    {{/hasrows}}
</div>
